invariant: INV-41
file: src/rsa_mont64_blocks.c
catches: rsa_blocks_equiv_test
reason: the square's words of 2a drop the top bit of each word, the bit
  that moves into the word above, so a row's words are short by a power
  of two whenever that bit is set. bin/rsa_blocks_equiv_test holds
  rsa_mont64_blocks_square to the blocks' multiplication of a by itself at
  every multiple of 4 words, and to the loops above 16 words, where
  rsa_mont64_mont_square runs it.

--- old
        v[j] = (a[j] << 1) | moved;
--- new
        v[j] = (a[j] << 1) | (moved & 0);
